id: DRAFT-conan-cmaketools-transitive-includedirs
trigger_tool: conan|cmake
phase: testing,packaging
error_signature: fatal error.*file not found.*#include|Could not find a package configuration file|cpp_info.*includedirs.*empty
severity: 2
category: conan,packaging,build-system,testing
match_keywords: CMakeDeps,transitive dependency,includedirs,cpp_info.requires,find_package,INTERFACE_LINK_LIBRARIES,conan 2.29,test_package,header not found
title: CMakeDeps serializes empty includedirs for transitive dependencies - propagate them in package_info
root_cause: On the OHOS conan 2.29.1, CMakeDeps data files fill include dirs for DIRECT dependencies but leave the includedirs entry empty for TRANSITIVE ones (libdirs still filled). A package B that wraps dependency A passes conan find_package(B) and B::B correctly, but consumers including A headers through B::B get no -isystem for A and die on the first A include, even though the whole CMake target chain (B::B -> B_DEPS_TARGET -> A::A) is present.
affected_scope: every multi-level Conan dependency graph consumed with generators=CMakeDeps on this toolchain; typical symptom is the package library itself building fine while its test_package fails on a transitive header.
verification_cmd: conan install --requires B/x -g CMakeDeps, then grep INCLUDE_DIRS in the dependency data cmake file
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: package-info-explicit-include-propagation
rec_description: In the wrapper package package_info(), copy the dependency include dirs into the wrapper cpp_info so the always-direct wrapper target carries them, and keep cpp_info.requires for link propagation. Verify with conan install -g CMakeDeps before rerunning conan create.
rec_command: in package_info set cpp_info.requires to a::a and cpp_info.includedirs.extend(dependencies[a].cpp_info.includedirs)
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: cppinfo-include-propagation
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: direct-require-in-test-package
fallback_description: Declare the transitive dependency directly in the test_package conanfile in addition to tested_reference_str so its include dirs are filled; acceptable for tests but leaks the dependency version into the test package.
fallback_command: in requirements call requires(self.tested_reference_str) plus requires(a/1.2.3)
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: direct-test-require
forbid_1_pattern: copy.*headers.*into.*package|duplicate.*include.*tree
forbid_1_reason: Duplicating dependency headers breaks the dependency graph and double-maintains versions.
forbid_1_consequence: Consumer picks stale headers and include/link mismatches.
forbid_2_pattern: include_directories.*storage.*p.*include|hardcoded.*package.*folder
forbid_2_reason: Hardcoded cache paths only work on the authoring machine.
forbid_2_consequence: CI and other machines fail on nonexistent paths.
forbid_3_pattern: global.*include.*env|CPATH.*workaround
forbid_3_reason: Environment-based include injection escapes Conan dependency management.
forbid_3_consequence: Other packages silently depend on leaked environment state.
principles: P003,P012
causes: null
caused_by: null
similar_to: E216,E221,E217
conflicts_with: null
prerequisite_of: null
